 of things and so we'll have to wait  to see i do think on balance though you  know we're always weighing risks and  benefits and i think during a period the  period of time where there was so much  uncertainty  certainly  it was worth the potential risk of  deficits in the microbiome to avoid the  sure risk of potential exposure to covid  for young and unvaccinated children  thank you  so do oncology nutritionists recommend  butyrate for patients with graft versus  host disease  so butyrate itself isn't recommended and  part of the reason it isn't recommended  is it really honestly just stinks  butyrate uh i can't believe i'm gonna  say this on a webinar butyrate smells  like farts and so nobody wants to take  it even mice don't want to eat it um and  that's part of why this workaround has  arisen which is giving people fiber so  that butyrate can be made when the fiber  is metabolized  the other challenge is of course  butyrate is actually a small molecule if  you remember what it looks like tiny  short chain fatty acid so it can also be  absorbed very high in the in the gi  tract which means that it may not get  down to the parts of the intestine where  graph versus host disease is important  uh but absolutely it has been  investigated you know people have  thought about are there ways to  formulate butyrate into like a super  um  old factory contained capsule so people  can take it  but it hasn't quite hit prime time yet  all right thank you um last question  that we have time for today since you  talked about boosting regulatory t cells  i imagine there have been studies also  regarding the microbiome and  inflammatory diseases  um specifically like ulcerative colitis  and crohn's  yeah so there have been extensive  studies on ulcerative colitis and  crohn's disease which are two different  flavors of inflammatory bowel disease  these diseases for those who aren't  familiar are caused by our immune  systems attacking our guts and the two  diseases are slightly different from one  another but actually share some  similarities there have been like i said  extensive studies in this regard a lot  of people have actually postulated that  fecal microbiota transplant might be  helpful in changing the microbiomes of  these individuals to try and increase  regulatory t cell proliferation and  suppress inflammation  that's actually some of the work where  it's been found that  while a fecal microbiota transplantation  might help people for a while the effect  seems to go away and we wonder if our  findings that donor strains don't really  engraft for the long term might be  responsible for this finding and so  there are studies underway with both  fecal microbiota transplant and  probiotics live bacterial therapies to  to give people those therapies on a  routine basis to try and suppress  inflammation  so i anticipate that there will continue  to be exciting research in this realm i  will say from a physician perspective if  we could find a way to find the  molecules that are actually responsible  for  modulating the immune system and doing  much more than just inducing t-reg  proliferation i'd much rather develop  those molecules into medications that we  can give patients  rather than taking the risk of giving  somebody  a fecal microbiota transplant filled  with lots of known and many more unknown  bacteria where i could possibly be  introducing a pathogen and so i would  say the field is really moving in the  direction of thinking about what the  molecules are that the microbes use to  engage in crosstalk and then leveraging  those as potential drug-like compounds  perfect thank you so much i think that's  all the questions that we have  time for today so  we're going to need to wrap up um but if  you'd like to learn more from dr bot and  the rest of the genetics faculty we  encourage you to join our genetics and  genomics program you have more than 90  hours of content to learn from them as  well as access to videos and exercises  to sharpen your skills and a link to the  recording of this session will be  emailed to you soon so feel free to  revisit this content once again thank  you for joining us and we hope you have  a great week  we hope to see you again in future  sessions and thank you so much dr bot  for joining us today this is a great  presentation we appreciate it  thank you very much have a great day  everyone  you
 

